# Single-store WooCommerce storefront

## Product
- One Next.js storefront for one WooCommerce / WordPress shop.
- Backend is WooCommerce REST API (`wc/v3`) via Axios in `lib/api/client.ts`.
- Design (layout, theme, motion, UI copy) lives in Next.js.
- Catalog data (products, categories, prices, stock, featured) comes only from WooCommerce admin via the API. Do not hardcode products.
- If Woo credentials are unset or the API fails, product lists render empty and design fallbacks in `data/site.json` still apply for theme/chrome.
- Scope: home, product listing, collection, product detail, cart, checkout. No signup, onboarding, or admin UI in this app. No ACF.

## Design system
- Theme tokens live in `data/site.json` under `theme.light` and `theme.dark`.
- Tokens are applied as CSS variables through `lib/theme.ts`.
- Light/dark mode is user-toggleable via `ThemeModeProvider`.
- Homepage section composition is fixed in Next components (`HomeSections`).

## Architecture boundaries
- `getSiteSettings()` uses Next design config (`data/site.json`) for branding, hero, footer, and contact. Currency (and site URL) may be overlaid from Woo when available.
- Components receive data via props or `useStore()`. Only pages, the provider, and the cart store talk to `lib/api`.
- Keep consumer keys server-side. Never import the Woo client into client components.
- Keep UI text and comments free of em dashes.
